1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Night outside the house
Penny arrives at the abandoned house. The camera cranes down from the street.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:18,000
In through the open door
Penny walks in; the main door closes and locks. She climbs the eighteen-step stair.

3
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Three clues: 257
Train 2, clock 5, blocks 7. The keypad opens the real Toy Room doors.

4
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:36,000
The toy chest
The red wind-up button opens the lid. Woody, Jessie and Bullseye climb out alive.

5
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Downstairs together
The toys follow Penny through a graph of doorway nodes and down the stairs.

6
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Cupboard rescue
Jessie mounts Bullseye, he jumps, she opens the wardrobe and Buzz flies out.

7
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:10,000
The locked main door
Penny tries the door. Buzz flies into position; L fires a nearest-hit laser and the door breaks.

8
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Morning escape
Everyone leaves the house. The fog thins, the sun rises and the camera pulls back.

9
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Free exploration
The story stays open in daylight. Adiba Tahsin / 2107031 / CSE-4102.

10
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:38,000
Live character takeover
Woody follows your input while the others keep accompanying Penny. Zero releases ownership.

11
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:44,000
Gouraud shading
Lighting is evaluated at vertices and interpolated across triangles.

12
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Phong shading
Interpolated normals are normalised before per-fragment illumination.

13
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Analytic ray tracing
A BVH accelerates exact primitive hits, shadows, mirror paths and straight transparency.
